1
00:00:07,001 --> 00:00:09,538
Whiskers and the Wobbly Bicycle.

2
00:00:21,989 --> 00:00:25,787
One windy spring morning, somebody tapped on the window.

3
00:00:29,487 --> 00:00:31,894
Go away. I'm closed for napping.

4
00:00:34,719 --> 00:00:37,946
Special delivery for Miss Luna! Airmail from Amsterdam!

5
00:00:38,146 --> 00:00:41,585
It's from my cousin Bram! He lives on a boat, on the canals!

6
00:00:41,785 --> 00:00:46,314
Come to the Tulip Parade! The whole city rides bicycles covered in flowers!

7
00:00:46,514 --> 00:00:50,970
Bicycles? Cats don't ride bicycles. Cats ride sofas.

8
00:00:51,170 --> 00:00:55,310
And there's a cheese market. And stroopwafels, waffles with syrup inside!

9
00:00:58,136 --> 00:00:59,707
Where is my suitcase?

10
00:00:59,907 --> 00:01:02,523
Hop into my basket. I'm flying that way!

11
00:01:08,849 --> 00:01:12,733
So the stork carried them over the sea, above the clouds.

12
00:01:19,934 --> 00:01:23,157
Please don't drop us. I'm a very fragile cat.

13
00:01:27,295 --> 00:01:29,672
Surprise! Did you really think I'd miss this?

14
00:01:32,497 --> 00:01:36,118
Pip! Oh look, tulip fields! Like a giant rainbow blanket!

15
00:01:44,194 --> 00:01:46,895
Hello, windmills! They're waving at us!

16
00:01:52,346 --> 00:01:57,944
In Amsterdam, tall skinny houses lined the canals, and bicycles were everywhere.

17
00:02:03,394 --> 00:02:05,923
Whoa! Why is everybody ringing at me?

18
00:02:10,498 --> 00:02:12,520
Luna! Over here, on the houseboat!

19
00:02:16,658 --> 00:02:20,501
Welcome, cousins! Whiskers, orange is the luckiest colour in Holland!

20
00:02:20,701 --> 00:02:23,355
Finally. A city that understands me.

21
00:02:27,055 --> 00:02:32,599
Then Bram took them to the cheese market, piled high with big yellow cheeses.

22
00:02:36,299 --> 00:02:39,579
Hallo, little cats! A warm stroopwafel for each of you!

23
00:02:45,030 --> 00:02:48,863
Syrup... inside a waffle? This country is a genius.

24
00:02:51,688 --> 00:02:54,642
Careful, Whiskers! Not that cheese, it's the biggest one!

25
00:03:07,093 --> 00:03:10,474
I did that on purpose. I was testing the wheels.

26
00:03:10,674 --> 00:03:13,571
Ha! If you can ride a cheese, you can ride a bicycle!

27
00:03:16,834 --> 00:03:21,040
So Bram found three little bicycles, and the lesson began.

28
00:03:26,491 --> 00:03:28,630
Look, Whiskers! It's just like flying!

29
00:03:36,706 --> 00:03:39,259
Left, right, left... which way is up?

30
00:03:45,147 --> 00:03:48,984
That's it. I give up. Cats are not made for bicycles.

31
00:03:53,122 --> 00:03:57,572
That evening, Whiskers sat by the canal all alone, still dripping.

32
00:04:02,148 --> 00:04:06,567
Every kitten in Amsterdam falls in the canal once. I fell in three times!

33
00:04:06,767 --> 00:04:10,276
Falling off just means you're learning. The trick is getting back on.

34
00:04:10,476 --> 00:04:13,474
And this time, I'll hold on to your seat. I promise.

35
00:04:21,550 --> 00:04:24,187
Luna, I'm doing it! Keep holding on!

36
00:04:24,387 --> 00:04:27,430
I let go ages ago! You're riding all by yourself!

37
00:04:33,755 --> 00:04:35,785
I'm riding! I'm really riding!

38
00:04:38,611 --> 00:04:42,434
The next morning, the Tulip Parade rolled through the city.

39
00:04:53,136 --> 00:04:54,738
Hooray for the orange cat!

40
00:04:54,938 --> 00:04:56,805
Faster, Whiskers! Ring the bell!

41
00:05:01,380 --> 00:05:03,937
Look, Luna! Not one single wobble!

42
00:05:15,951 --> 00:05:19,641
That night, Joost flew the three friends all the way home.

43
00:05:22,904 --> 00:05:25,455
Goodbye, little cyclists! Keep on pedalling!

44
00:05:25,655 --> 00:05:28,242
Whiskers, will you teach me to ride a bicycle?

45
00:05:28,442 --> 00:05:32,815
Sure, Pip. Lesson one, you fall in. Lesson two, you get back on.

46
00:05:38,703 --> 00:05:43,424
Because everybody wobbles at first. The brave part is getting back on.

